ELUCIDATION
OF
REGIONAL REGULATION OF DHARMASRAYA REGENCY
NUMBER 16 OF 2018
CONCERNING
WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION

I. GENERAL
Children are a trust as well as a gift from God Almighty, which we must always protect because inherent in them are dignity, honor, and rights as human beings that must be upheld. Children's human rights are part of human rights contained in the 1945 Constitution and the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child. From the perspective of national and state life, children are the future of the nation and the next generation of the nation's ideals, so that every child has the right to survival, growth, and development, to participate and has the right to protection from acts of violence and discrimination as well as civil rights and freedoms.

Likewise with women, from women are expected to be born children who are healthy, strong, resilient, of noble character, potential and quality. Through the role of women in the family, society and state will be born resilient generations who will continue the nation's ideals. As citizens of Indonesia, women also have the right to improve quality and develop themselves according to their abilities, dignity and honor.

Women and children need to be protected from acts of discrimination and acts of violence whether physical, psychological, mental, sexual and neglect. Because of their physical weakness compared to men and adults and because of women's nature itself, women and children often become objects of venting desires, anger, economic exploitation, violence (physical, psychological and sexual), cruelty, neglect, and so on. As assets and hope of the nation and state, children need to be given protection and safeguarded from all forms of acts of violence that will hinder their growth and development.

To realize women's empowerment and child protection, support from laws and regulations is needed that can guarantee its implementation.

Although the protection of women's and children's rights has been regulated in national level laws and regulations, the fulfillment of women's and children's constitutional rights and the improvement of the quality of life of women and children is one of the mandatory affairs that is the duty, authority and responsibility of the Regional Government, therefore in providing protection to women and children, the Regional Government needs to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.

This Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and Child Protection regulates the following scope: a. rights of women and children;
b. obligations;
c. improvement of women's quality of life;
d. protection of women and children;
e. improvement of family quality;
f. gender and child data system;
g. fulfillment of children's rights;
h. child-friendly regency; and
i. guidance and supervision.

Article 69
(1) The policy for the development of CFC is directed towards the fulfillment of Children's rights which are divided into 5 (five) groups, comprising: a. civil rights and freedoms;
b. family environment and alternative care; c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, utilization of leisure time, and cultural activities; and
e. special protection.
(2) Further provisions regarding the policy for the development of CFC as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 3
Women's Empowerment and Child Protection aims to: a. serve as a guideline for local government in planning, policies and strategies for the protection of women and children;
b. protect women and children from actions, decisions and policies that violate the rights of women and children; c. prevent violations of the rights of women and children;
d. increase empowerment of women and children;
e. enhance the role and value of local wisdom and the role of customs in the protection of women and children; and f. enhance the role of government and non-government institutions in the region in efforts to protect women and children.

